>> title: Wonton Soup
>> category: Soups
>> tags: pork, shrimp, dumpling, chinese, stovetop
>> counters: Takeout Counter, One Pot
>> aka: wonton soup, won ton soup, wantan soup, huntun tang, 雲吞麵湯, 餛飩湯
>> pairs-with: egg-rolls
>> servings: 4
>> time: 1 hr

>> step: mix one way until sticky, chill 20 min
Mix @ground pork{8%oz}(225 g; not lean) with @raw shrimp{4%oz}(115 g; peeled and chopped), @light soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @Shaoxing wine{2%tsp}, @toasted sesame oil{1%tsp}, @fresh ginger{2%tsp}(grated), @scallions{2}(finely sliced), and @white pepper{1/4%tsp}, stirring in one direction until it turns sticky and holds together, then ~chill{20%min}.

>> step: wrap, a scant teaspoon each
Wrap a scant teaspoon of @&(~1)filling{} in each of @wonton wrappers{40}(thin, square), wetting two edges and pinching out the air.

>> step: boil 4 min, until they float and swell
Boil @&(~1)wontons{} in a wide #pot{} of water, in two batches, for ~boil{4%min} — they are done when they float and the wrapper goes translucent at the seam.

>> step: simmer the broth 10 min
Simmer @chicken stock{6%cups}(1.4 L) with @fresh ginger{2%slices}(coin-sized), @light soy sauce{1%Tbs}, and @kosher salt{1/2%tsp} for ~simmer{10%min}.

>> step: ladle over, greens in the bowl
Ladle @&(~1)broth{} over @&(~2)wontons{} in warmed bowls with @baby bok choy{4%heads}(halved, wilted in the broth), @scallions{2}(sliced), and @toasted sesame oil{1/2%tsp}.
